                               rdfs:label "additionalNumberOfGuests".
shema:additionalProperty shema:domainIncludes shema:Place,
                                              shema:QualitativeValue,
                                              shema:QuantitativeValue,
                                              shema:Product;
                         shema:rangeIncludes shema:PropertyValue;
                         a rdf:Property;
                         rdfs:comment """A property-value pair representing an additional characteristics of the entitity, e.g. a product feature or another characteristic for which there is no matching property in schema.org.<br/><br/>

Note: Publishers should be aware that applications designed to use specific schema.org properties (e.g. http://schema.org/width, http://schema.org/color, http://schema.org/gtin13, ...) will typically expect such data to be provided using those properties, rather than using the generic property/value mechanism.""";
                         rdfs:label "additionalProperty".
shema:additionalType shema:domainIncludes shema:Thing;
                     shema:rangeIncludes shema:URL;
                     a rdf:Property;
                     rdfs:comment "An additional type for the item, typically used for adding more specific types from external vocabularies in microdata syntax. This is a relationship between something and a class that the thing is in. In RDFa syntax, it is better to use the native RDFa syntax - the 'typeof' attribute - for multiple types. Schema.org tools may have only weaker understanding of extra types, in particular those defined externally.";
                     rdfs:label "additionalType";
                     rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:type.
shema:address shema:domainIncludes shema:Place,
